    {
      "unit_id": 70,
      "text": "Solutions in",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "parent_id": 0,
      "subtype": "sectionheader"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 71,
      "text": "V 11 2 [0, 1] The solution of the problem is considered in the V 11 2 [0, 1]. We define Y : V 11 2 [0, 1] → V 1 2 [0, 1]",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 72,
      "text": "as",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 73,
      "text": "Yh(τ) = h (x) (τ) + a 1 (τ)h (ix) (τ) + a 2 (τ)h (viii) (τ) + a 3 (τ)h (vii) (τ) +a 4 (τ)h (vi) (τ) + a 5 (τ)h (v) (τ) + a 6 (τ)h (iv) (τ) + a 7 (τ)h (τ) +a 8 (τ)h (τ) + a 9 (τ)h (τ) + a 10 (τ)h(τ).",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 74,
      "text": "The model problem changes to the following problem:",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 75,
      "text": "Yh = M(τ), τ ∈ [0, 1],(4)",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 76,
      "text": "with the following boundary conditions:",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 77,
      "text": "h(a) = 0, h(b) = 0, h (a) = 0, h (b) = 0, h (iv) (a) = 0, h (iv) (b) = 0, h (vi) (a) = 0, h (vi) (b) = 0, h (viii) (a) = 0, h (viii) (b) = 0.",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 78,
      "text": "Theorem 1. Y is a bounded linear operator.",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 79,
      "text": "Proof.We need to show Yh 2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 80,
      "text": "V 1 2 ≤ M h 2 V 11 2",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 81,
      "text": ", where M > 0. We acquire",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 82,
      "text": "Yh 2 V 1 2 = Yh, Yh V 1 2 = 1 0 Yh(τ) 2 + Yh (τ) 2 dτ",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 83,
      "text": "by Equations ( 1) and ( 2).We obtain",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 84,
      "text": "h(τ) = h(•), P τ (•) V 11 2 and Yh(τ) = h(•), YP τ (•) V 11 2",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 85,
      "text": ", by reproducing property.Thus, we reach",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
