    },
    {
      "unit_id": 86,
      "text": "|Yh(τ)| ≤ h V 11 2 YP τ V 11 2 = M 1 h V 11 2 ,",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 87,
      "text": "where M 1 > 0. Therefore, we find",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 88,
      "text": "1 0 [(Yh) (τ)] 2 dτ ≤ M 2 1 h 2 V 11 2 . Since (Yh) (τ) = h(•), (YP η ) (•) V 11 2 , then (Yh) (η) ≤ h V 11 2 (YP τ ) V 11 2 = M 2 f V 11 2 ,",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 89,
      "text": "where M 2 > 0. Therefore, we reach",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 90,
      "text": "(Yh) (τ) 2 ≤ M 2 2 h 2 V 11 2 and 1 0 (Yh) (τ) 2 dτ ≤ M 2 2 h 2 V 11 2 .",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 91,
      "text": "Finally, we obtain",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 92,
      "text": "Yh 2 V 1 2 ≤ 1 0 [(Yh) (τ)] 2 + (Yh) (τ) 2 dτ ≤ M 2 1 + M 2 2 h 2 V 11 2 = M h 2 V 11 2 ,",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 93,
      "text": "where",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 94,
      "text": "M = M 2 1 + M 2 2 > 0.",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 95,
      "text": "The Main Results",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 70,
      "subtype": "sectionheader"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 96,
      "text": "Let",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 97,
      "text": "ϕ i (τ) = T τ i (τ) and ψ i (τ) = Y * ϕ i (τ), Y * is an adjoint operator of Y. The orthonormal system Ψ i (τ) ∞ i=1 of V 11",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 98,
      "text": "2 [0, 1] can be obtained as:",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 99,
      "text": "ψ i (τ) = i ∑ k=1 β ik ψ k (τ), (β ii > 0, i = 1, 2, . . .). (5",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 100,
      "text": ")",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 101,
      "text": "Theorem 2. Let {τ i } ∞ i=1 be dense in [0, 1] and ψ i (τ) = Y ς T τ (ς)| ς=τ i . Then, the sequence {ψ i (τ)} ∞ i=1 is a complete system in V 11 2 [0, 1].",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 102,
      "text": "Proof.We get",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 103,
      "text": "ψ i (τ) = (Y * ϕ i )(τ) = (Y * ϕ i )(ς), T τ (ς) = ϕ i )(ς), YςT τ (ς) = Y ς T τ (ς)| ς=τ i . We know that ψ i (τ) ∈ V 11 2 [0, 1]. For each fixed h(τ) ∈ V 11 2 [0, 1], let h(τ), ψ i (η) = 0, (i = 1, 2, . . .), h(τ), (Y * ϕ i )(τ) = Yh(•), ϕ i (•) = (Yh)(τ i ) = 0. {τ i } ∞ i=1 is dense in [0, 1]. Thus, (Yh)(τ) = 0. h ≡ 0 by the Y −1 . Theorem 3. If h(τ) is the exact solution of Equation (4), then h = ∞ ∑ i=1 i ∑ k=1 β ik M(τ k )ψ i (τ),(6)",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 104,
      "text": "where",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 105,
      "text": "{(τ i )} ∞ i=1 is dense in [0, 1].",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 106,
      "text": "Proof.We obtain",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 107,
      "text": "h(τ) = ∞ ∑ i=1 h(τ), ψ i (τ) V 11 2 ψ i (τ) = ∞ ∑ i=1 i ∑ k=1 β ik h(τ), Ψ k (τ) V 11 2 ψ i (τ) = ∞ ∑ i=1 i ∑ k=1 β ik h(τ), Y * ϕ k (τ) V 11 2 ψ i (τ) = ∞ ∑ i=1 i ∑ k=1 β ik Yh(τ), ϕ k (η) V 1 2 ψ i (τ) = ∞ ∑ i=1 i ∑ k=1 β ik Yh(τ k )ψ i (τ) = ∞ ∑ i=1 i ∑ k=1 β ik M(τ k )ψ i (η),",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 108,
      "text": "by Equation ( 5) and the uniqueness of solution of Equation ( 4).",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 109,
      "text": "The approximate solution h n can be obtained by:",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 110,
      "text": "h n = n ∑ i=1 i ∑ k=1 β ik M(τ k )ψ i (τ).(7)",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 3,
      "parent_id": 95,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 111,
      "text": "Numerical Results",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "parent_id": 0,
      "subtype": "sectionheader"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 112,
      "text": "Example 1.We consider the following tenth-order equation as:",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 113,
      "text": "q (10) (τ) = −(80 + 19τ + τ 2 ) exp(τ), 0 ≤ τ ≤ 1,",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 114,
      "text": "with boundary conditions: q(0) = 0, q(1) = 0, q (0) = 0, q (1) = −4 exp(1),",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 115,
      "text": "q (iv) (0) = −8, q (iv) (1) = −16 exp(1), q (vi) (0) = −24, q (vi) (1) = −36 exp(1), q (viii) (0) = −48, q (viii) (1) = −64 exp(1).",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 116,
      "text": "The exact solution to the above boundary value problem is given by [1]:",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 117,
      "text": "q(τ) = τ(1 − τ) exp(τ).",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 118,
      "text": "We need to homogenize the boundary conditions to apply the reproducing kernel Hilbert space method:",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 119,
      "text": "r 1 (x) = c 1 + c 2 x + c 3 x 2 + c 4 x 3 + c 5 x 4 +c 6 x 5 + c 7 x 6 + c 8 x 7 + c 9 x 8 + c 10 x 9 s 1 = c 1 = 0, s 2 = 2c 3 = 0, s 3 = 24c 5 = −8, s 4 = 720c 7 = −24, s 5 = 40, 320c 9 = −48, s 6 = c 1 + c 2 + c 3 + c 4 + c 5 + c 6 + c 7 + c 8 + c 9 + c 10 = 0, s 7 =",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 120,
      "text": "= −64e,                      c 1 = 0, c 2 = −24",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 121,
      "text": "                    ",
      "type": "equation",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "formula"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 122,
      "text": "Therefore, we obtain r 1 (x) = − 1 113, 400",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 123,
      "text": "x (20x",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "level": 2,
      "parent_id": 111,
      "subtype": "body"
    },
    {
      "unit_id": 124,
